{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:7f57d756f8a46c91","name":"Zephyr-G Swoop Bike","source":{"id":"source:reference-7f57d756f8a46c91","title":"Zephyr-G Swoop Bike","revision":19613,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:16:56Z","sha256":"69f0e8f821445d977fb84669b4747b45f6c9d43809936d33ab8f0d59511ebf0d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19613","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Zephyr-G%20Swoop%20Bike&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-7f57d756f8a46c91","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Zephyr-G Swoop Bike is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder Bike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder_Bike"}," designed for sport racing, but sturdy enough to be used as a utility craft as well. Like most swoops, it emphasizes speed and power over safety and maneuverability. The Zephyr-G has inhibitors that prevent it from hovering more than 6 meters above the ground, but if those are disabled (",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," DC 15), it can rise to nearly a kilometer. It's also possible to mount ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pistols"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pistols","referenceId":"reference:e660061b7b03b794"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rifles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rifles","referenceId":"reference:a6ebe3ecc8b0b281"}," to the swoop, though the frame lacks the bracing for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapons","referenceId":"reference:a2b1d4c4bac82300"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Zephyr-G has far more power than it needs, a feature that allows it to carry a passenger (uncomfortably unless the seat is modified) and some extra materials. Though stock models don't include any cargo capacity, it costs only 10 credits to add cargo panniers capable of holding 100 kg of gear. These factors are a large part of why it proved popular with fringe-world buyers, despite its relatively slow speed for a swoop. (",{"tag":"a","children":["Owen Lars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Owen_Lars?action=edit&redlink=1"}," owned a Zephyr-G, which ",{"tag":"a","children":["Anakin Skywalker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Anakin_Skywalker","referenceId":"reference:e7c68f75d23b428e"}," borrowed to search for his mother.)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Zephyr-G Swoop Bike Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 17; +2 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 50; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 5; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 22